# More info: https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file
#
# Allowlist, not a denylist. The Dockerfile packages a prebuilt binary again
# (CI cross-compiles on the runner, see .github/workflows/ci.yml), so the Go
# source no longer needs to reach the build context, only dist/manager-<arch>.
#
# This restores the pre-2026-07-30 shape. It became a denylist while the
# Dockerfile compiled from source in a multi-stage build, which put `dist` on
# the ignore list, and that silently breaks `COPY dist/manager-${TARGETARCH}`.
**
!dist/manager-*
